  "result": "Perfect! All 168 tests pass. I've successfully added voucher support to invoices:\n\n**New in `src/errors.js`:**\n- `VOUCHER_EXISTS` \u2014 invoice already has a voucher applied\n\n**Updated `src/invoices.js`:**\n\n**Updated `invoiceTotals()`** now returns:\n```javascript\n{ subtotal, discount, vat, voucher, total }\n```\nWhere:\n- `voucher` = the voucher amount (0 if none)\n- `total` = subtotal - discount + vat - voucher (clamped at 0)\n\n**New `applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })` function:**\n- Applies a fixed amount voucher to draft invoices only\n- Validates:\n  - Status is 'draft' (NOT_DRAFT error)\n  - No voucher already applied (VOUCHER_EXISTS error)\n  - Amount is positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID error)\n- Sets `invoice.voucher = { code, amount }`\n- Never mutates input invoice\n- Returns new invoice with voucher applied\n\n**9 new tests** covering:\n- Voucher field in invoiceTotals\n- Voucher calculation (amount deducted from total)\n- Applying voucher to draft invoices\n- Draft-only enforcement\n- One-voucher-per-invoice enforcement\n- Amount validation (positive integer)\n- Input immutability\n- Voucher applied after discount and VAT\n- Total clamped at 0 (even if voucher exceeds total)\n\n**Invoice total formula:**\n```\ntotal = max(0, subtotal - discount + vat - voucher)\n```\n\nFull invoice lifecycle now complete: draft \u2192 add lines/discount/voucher \u2192 issue \u2192 record payments \u2192 track due date \u2713",
